<title>POLAND: Polish crop ratings slightly better in June 11-20.</title>
<headline>Polish crop ratings slightly better in June 11-20.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Meteorology and Water Management Institute (IMGW) said crop evaluations in the second 10 days of June were slightly better than the previous 10-day period and stayed above 1996 and five-year average levels.</p>
<p>Ratings are made three times a month based on the condition and development of crops on a scale of one to five, with five the highest grade.</p>
<p>POLISH CROP RATINGS   JUNE 20   JUNE 10  1996   5-YR AVG</p>
<p> Wheat (winter)	   3.6	3.5	3.6	3.5</p>
<p> Wheat (summer)	   3.6	3.6	3.6	3.4</p>
<p> Rye			  3.6	3.6	3.6	3.5</p>
<p> Barley (spring)	  3.7	3.6	3.6	3.4</p>
<p> Rapeseed (winter)	3.0	3.1	2.9	3.3</p>
<p> Oats			 3.6	3.6	3.6	3.4</p>
<p> Sugar beets		3.5	3.4	3.5	3.4</p>
<p> Potatoes		   3.6	3.4	3.5	3.4</p>
<p>--Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
